---
description: Documentation language and structure rules
globs: "**/*.{md,mdc}"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Write project docs in English; only language-suffixed docs and rules enforcing another language may differ. Translation files are not docs.
- Search and update existing docs before creating new files.
- Choose architecture, domains, engineering, operations, reference, or prompts per `core/docs/engineering/documentation-standards.md`.
- Keep docs short and link instead of duplicating; update section README navigation when files move or are added.
- Repo docs are stable source-of-truth; Obsidian is for research/ideas (`core/docs/engineering/obsidian-usage.md`).
- Use kebab-case filenames, one H1, and required title/owner/type/scope/status frontmatter.
